- Story & Context: Legend says that after the authority raids shut the power down forever, the coastal tides flooded the lower sectors of the accelerator tunnel, turning the dancefloor into a saltwater lagoon. Local kids who swim into the dark concrete pipe swear they can still hear the residual magnetic resonance of old school rhymes trapped in the barnacle-crusted brass pipes. The track closes the EP with a haunting, slow-tempo chant over ambient ocean swells and choked sax echoes, asking what remains of a culture when the lights burn out. "If you put your ear to the copper track, the sun never sets and the drum comes back," whispers Chrysalis over the fading vinyl hiss.
